{#-
  ansible/inventory/graph_lab_run_binding.yml.j2 -- MAIN's frozen per-run binding for ANY lab (codex-tick302,
  generalized codex-tick350). It is rendered by the ONE declared render entry
  testing/e2e/inventory_binding/render_run_binding.yml (the controller's managed generation; in-memory render, then the
  entry's publication lifecycle: publish / unchanged reapply / interrupted-publication resume / explicit revision
  transition / conflict refusal) to <run>/.work/inventory/<lab>/20-binding.yml (0600), next to 10-lab.yml (a byte copy
  of the lab file); its receipt (binding, data and lab sha256) lies outside the -i directory. Every leg of the run
  passes that ONE directory as `-i`.
  What the RENDER guarantees (mandatory; a missing one fails the render): rb_bs, rb_repo_root, rb_run (declared top keys only),
  rb_derived (deployment_identity from the lab file through the canonical filter, lab_sha256, controller values, the
  loader's bound lab target inputs), and the DERIVED paths (owner_key / owner_pubkey for every run host with an effective
  owner; bundle_dir = bound prereq_bundle_root / bundle.leaf); undeclared roles / groups / host keys, supplied derived
  roles and supplied derived inputs refuse. Per-host ROLES are optional data: role COMPLETENESS is enforced by each
  consuming leg (e.g. target_prereq's preservation expectation; observe.yml an absent obs_paths), never by this
  template. The binding carries no all.vars: lme_deployment_identity is declared ONCE in the lab file (codex-tick360).

  GENERIC (codex-tick350 GRAPH-BINDING-TEMPLATE-TOPOLOGY): this file is a THIN CALLER of the generic macros
  ansible/inventory/macros/run_binding.j2. It names no machine, group, role var or key path: machines and placement are
  INVENTORY DATA (the lab's desired topology stays in its lab file, e.g. graph_lab_example.yml; per-run values in
  rb_run). Renaming, adding or removing a target is a data change only
  (testing/e2e/inventory_binding/run_binding.cases.yml).
  The file name is historical (the graph lab was its first user); a rename is a separate, MAIN-ordered move because
  graph_lab_example.yml and the run receipts cite it.
  The former staged exception (gb_binding_stage locate | final) is RETIRED: owner_key / owner_pubkey are no longer
  inputs; they are DERIVED here from the J-KEY producer contract's location rule (owner_key.location_rule_rel), the
  same rule the producer renders and checks (JKEY-LOCATION). The producer's read-only locate op stays a diagnostic.

  Inputs (template vars, all required):
    rb_bs          the RESOLVED rh.controller.bootstrap (names: target_inputs role -> var, target_group, role_groups,
                   root_var / owner_var; the J-KEY contract owner_key), obtained by the render entry through the
                   resolve-only path (resolve_policy -> podman resolve) over the lab copy -- never resolve_harness.yml,
                   whose controller root / owner this binding supplies.
                   SEQUENCING: rendering requires C1's owner_key node (incl. location_rule_rel, storage.pub_suffix:
                   JK-6) and inventory.role_groups; until then the render fails (no partial binding).
    rb_repo_root   the controller checkout (rh_repo_root; the location rule's work-root anchor)
    rb_run         the per-run data: ONLY the declared top keys (rb_bs.run_binding.run_data.top, r5f): controller
                   {operation, inputs?} (REQUIRED; no default operation) and hosts.<alias> {member_of?, roles (run-time
                   values only, e.g. privileged_key), bundle {leaf}?, address?, global_override?, observed?} (shape:
                   macros/run_binding.j2 header).
    rb_derived     the render entry's derived values: deployment_identity (null only for an identity_nullable
                   controller operation: diagnostic attribution, never proof), lab_sha256, controller {toolchain_root,
                   owner, operation, inputs}, bound. The render entry runs under either declared launch
                   (run_binding.launches: managed seed `run`, or the genesis builder stage) -- this template is the same.
-#}
{% import 'macros/run_binding.j2' as rb with context %}
{{ rb.binding(rb_bs | mandatory, rb_repo_root | mandatory, rb_run | mandatory, rb_derived | mandatory) }}
